The api serves its routes without an `/api` prefix. nginx has this location:

```nginx
location /api/ {
    proxy_pass http://api:3000/;
}
```

Statement: "A request for `/api/orders?status=new` reaches the api as `/orders?status=new`."

The forwarded headers are set at server level, and the reports location adds one header of its own:

```nginx
server {
    proxy_set_header Host              $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP         $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For   $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

    location /api/reports/ {
        proxy_set_header Connection "";
        proxy_read_timeout 300s;
        proxy_pass http://api/reports/;
    }
}
```

Statement: "Requests to `/api/reports/` still carry `X-Real-IP` and `X-Forwarded-Proto`, because the location only adds one more header."
